# Private functions
  @fn periodTicks(period, resolution)  @ 29-32
  -- Note arithmetic
  @fn interval(a, b)  @ 38-40
      -- Cents between two notes' realised pitches. The microtonal offset already rides
      -- in detune, so this is pure note arithmetic -- no temper needed.
  @fn displaced(note, cents)  @ 44-46
      -- The inverse: a note displaced by cents, placed back on (pitch, detune). A pitch demand is
      -- cents here and never notation steps. see design/sounding-anchor.md § The notation is not a derivation input
  @fn inherited(src, cents)  @ 50-52
      -- The name that rides with it: the source's intent moved by the cents this note stands off it.
      -- A source carrying none derives none, and the note reads as it sounds; see design/sounding-anchor.md § What the note remembers
  @fn retrig(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 56-76
      @contract  retrig tiles the host window with evenly-spaced same-pitch fxNotes; every hit is derived  @ 54
      @contract  velocity ramps params.ramp per tile from the host vel, clamped 1..127; detune inherited verbatim  @ 55
  @fn trill(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 79-104
      @contract  trill alternates host pitch with a note `cents` off what it sounds; every hit derived  @ 78
  @fn playingAt(events, t)  @ 107-116
      -- Notes sounding at logical tick `t`, ascending by realised pitch (semitone*100 + detune cents).
  @fn arpIndex(count, dir, i)  @ 120-128
      -- Which voice of the active set step `i` plays, by direction. updown bounces without
      -- repeating the extremes (span 2*(n-1)); up/down wrap.
  @fn arp(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 133-154
      @contract  arp samples the sounding notes at each step (period QN), playing one by `dir`  @ 130
      @contract  dir up|down|updown cycles the current active set; an empty active set -> a rest  @ 131
      @contract  hits abut (endppq = next step), clamped to the window; vel/detune from the voice  @ 132
  @fn ostinato(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 158-179
      @contract  ostinato gates the sounding region notes by a stored pattern -- pattern gives onset/dur/vel, each voice its pitch/detune  @ 156
      @contract  every voice sounding at a gate onset emits (none -> rest); the pattern loops from the window start; no lengthPpq -> inert  @ 157
  @fn chordStamp(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 187-208
      -- Voices carry their authored detune (intent); on one channel only lane 1's detune realises via pb, so a
      -- microtonal chord sounds faithfully only in 12-ET -- the hand-authored-chord limit. see docs/tuning.md
  @fn sine(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 213-233
      @contract  sine -> delta breakpoints in the dest's own units; depth at 1/period QN, unit-naive  @ 210
      @contract  breakpoints at sine extrema, 'slow'-shaped; linear ramp-in over onset QN  @ 211
      @contract  a terminal 0 at window end eases the last extremum back -- shape, not reset (tm closes)  @ 212
  @fn slide(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 238-267
      @contract  slide glide-in -> lane-1 pb-delta; slur to target over `over` QN (tm closes the window)  @ 235
      @contract  target 'next' = interval to next same-lane note; 'fixed' = params.cents; pb-range clamps  @ 236
      @contract  no next note or unison target -> empty delta (channel untouched)  @ 237
  @fn curveAt(points, a)  @ 270-280
      -- Linear-interpolated normalized value at authored ppq `a`; points ascend in ppq, edges clamp flat.
  @fn lfo(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 285-313
      @contract  lfo tiles a normalized curve at 1/period QN, offset + scale map each val, unit-naive  @ 282
      @contract  breakpoints are a displacement from the dest's rest, which the augment fold lays them on  @ 283
      @contract  each cycle stretches the body lengthPpq -> period ticks; both window edges seeded  @ 284
  @fn velPattern(stream, host, params, ctx)  @ 317-334
      @contract  velPattern rewrites stream-note velocities by a pattern; other fields carry verbatim  @ 315
      @contract  pattern steps per distinct onset (a chord shares one step) and cycles; vel clamps 1..127  @ 316
  -- Generator registry
  -- Dest: a per-entry target, and what each target's numbers mean
  -- Region park predicate + windows
  -- Curve thinning (freeze to group)
  @fn ridesLinear(p)  @ 615
      -- A shape governs the segment to its *right*, so a point is safe to lose only if it and its
      -- predecessor both ride linearly; a missing shape counts as non-linear. see design/archive/fx-freeze.md § Freeze to group

# Functions held in tables
  @held fields.when(e)  @ 409

# Public API (generators.*)
  @api generators.glyphOf(kind)  @ 445-448
      -- One glyph per kind: a letter shapes notes, a wave mark paints a continuous stream. '?' is a
      -- kind the registry has lost. see docs/generators.md § Conventions
  @api generators.labelOf(kind)  @ 452-455
      -- One label per kind, and the one place a kind resolves to a name. A lost kind keeps its own
      -- name in the mark: `? arp` says which stage went missing where a bare `?` would not.
  @api generators.destOf(params)  @ 466-469
  @api generators.destProfile(dest)  @ 473-480
      -- Polarity is the controller's own, and its default rest says it: one resting mid-scale swings
      -- both ways, one at a rail only runs inward.
  @api generators.restFor(dest)  @ 484-486
      -- The resting base a continuous augment sums onto when the target carries no authored automation.
      -- Named despite being one line: the per-chain seed and per-channel fold must agree on this value.
  @api generators.destsFor(kind)  @ 489-496
      -- Every dest a kind can serve. Fewer than two is no choice at all, and earns no Dest row.
  @api generators.fieldRange(fd, dest)  @ 500-506
      -- A field's bounds in the target's own units: a magnitude spans rest outwards as far as the dest
      -- swings -- both ways if signed; anything else is fixed-unit and carries its bounds on the descriptor.
  @api generators.fieldsFor(entry)  @ 512-522
      -- The rows a stage shows: a synthesised Dest row where the kind can serve more than one target,
      -- then the kind's own fields. Synthesised once here rather than repeated per registry entry.
  @api generators.seed(kind)  @ 526-536
      -- A kind's default entry: the dest it seeds from, its fixed-unit defaults, and every quantity field
      -- resolved against that dest -- so one `frac` declaration reads correctly wherever it lands.
  @api generators.retarget(entry, dest)  @ 540-550
      -- Point an entry at another dest, carrying its magnitudes over as the same proportion of the new
      -- target's swing. Equal references (CC 10 -> CC 8, both resting at 64) leave every value untouched.
  @api generators.parksNotes(region)  @ 556-561
      -- A region parks its covered chord iff it carries a note-dest kind: the chain's final note stream
      -- stands in for the members (ownership by dest, not mode). A husk (no kinds) parks nothing.
  @api generators.continuousTargets(fx)  @ 565-572
      -- Continuous targets a chain touches: set keyed 'pb' | <cc number>, empty for a pure-note
      -- chain -- phase 5's per-target scopes key off it. see design/interval-dirt.md § phase 5
  @api generators.chainDestType(fx, target)  @ 576-584
      -- The fold mode a chain presents for one continuous target: replace if any live stage targeting it
      -- replaces, else augment -- a bypassed stage never counts, so it can't paint an overlapping chain's curve. see docs/generators.md § The chain
  @api generators.parkWindows(regions)  @ 589-609
      -- The single source for "what 4.5 parks over": a note window for a discrete-replace chord, a cc window
      -- per continuous cc target and a pb window per continuous pb target (both replace or augment).
  @api generators.thinCurve(points, tol)  @ 621-661
      -- Douglas-Peucker, measuring vertical deviation rather than perpendicular distance: perpendicular
      -- would need a ticks-per-cent aspect ratio, under which "tolerance in cents" means nothing.
      @contract  returns a new array of the input point tables themselves -- selects, never invents  @ 619
      @contract  tol bounds vertical error in the curve's own value unit; > tol keeps, == tol collapses  @ 620

